# Generated data IS committed -- see below for why it is not ignored.
#
# data/courses.json and data/courses_raw.json are build outputs, but they are
# also the product: the deployed site is a static bundle plus that JSON. A
# host like Netlify builds from the git checkout, so ignoring them means the
# build fails at `npm run sync-data`. The only alternative -- running the
# scraper during every deploy -- would hit apps.ualberta.ca on every push,
# which the scraper-etiquette rule in CLAUDE.md rules out.
#
# Committing courses_raw.json too (220K) means the parser can be re-run and
# iterated on without re-scraping the university's site at all.
#
# Still regenerate BOTH from scratch on every re-scrape; never hand-edit them.

# 6MB of cached page HTML -- a local dev convenience, not part of the product.
data/html_cache/

# Copied from data/courses.json at build time by frontend/scripts/sync-data.mjs.
frontend/public/courses.json

__pycache__/
*.pyc
venv/
.venv/
node_modules/
dist/
.DS_Store
